Placeholder so docker-compose.yml has a vault directory to mount when LEGEND_VAULT_PATH
is unset. Docker silently creates a *directory* at a missing bind-mount source, and an
accidental directory where a file was expected is how the SearXNG config broke once
already -- see deploy/searxng/up.sh. Keeping a real, committed directory here avoids
relying on that behaviour.

The `notes` tool family treats an empty vault as unavailable, which is a working state.
